NUL-terminate the buffers find_contact_from_impu() searches with strstr().

find_contact_from_impu() matches a dialog's contact against the IMPU's
bindings by copying both into 512-byte stack buffers (filter_default_port()
drops a ":5060" on the way) and then strstr()-ing them for '@', ':' and '~'.
filter_default_port() copies exactly len bytes and never terminates, so:

- the search AOR's buffer is never cleared: strstr() runs on into
  uninitialised stack until it happens on a NUL, and can match a '@' or '~'
  past the end of the AOR. memcheck reports "Conditional jump or move depends
  on uninitialised value(s) at find_contact_from_impu" with the origin at its
  stack frame, on every dialog callback for a contact;
- the bindings' buffer is memset each time round, so it is only terminated
  while the contact is shorter than 512 bytes;
- the ":5060" branch copied before checking the room, so a long contact
  overran the buffer.

Have filter_default_port() check the room first on both branches and
terminate what it copies, with the callers leaving a byte for the NUL.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_usrloc_scscf/contact_dlg_handlers.c b/src/modules/ims_usrloc_scscf/contact_dlg_handlers.c
index 0e7dd87174..6a1b98a4f5 100644
